# Testing and performance

- Every new feature comes with Catch2 tests in `tests/`, registered with CTest (`ctest --preset debug`).
- Test the edge cases: empty, full, single element, concurrent access, entity destroyed mid-iteration.
- Code must pass AddressSanitizer locally and TSan/UBSan in Linux CI.
- Benchmarks use Google Benchmark in `bench/`, run only in Release, and output JSON for comparison.
- When optimizing, record before/after numbers and add the result to `docs/performance-investigation.md`.
- Don't change a benchmark and the code it measures in the same commit.